   "speech": "On the evening I am speaking of, an event took place: a new patient appeared, the third in all. Even now, when I close my eyes, I can see him before me as if he were alive. He was a man of middle height, bald, with an important, slightly absent gaze, a curly fair little beard and a sharp nose. His build betrayed a tendency to stoutness, which made something of a contrast with his abrupt, impulsive movements. I also noticed two peculiarities that would not be worth mentioning had they not pointed to a severe degree of nervous disorder: a convulsive twitching of the eyelids and a ceaseless working of the fingers. Whether he sat or walked, spoke or was silent, the fingers of his hands bent and unbent uncontrollably, as though tangled in an invisible, sticky cobweb.",
